      "text": "To find the number of positive numbers not factorial tails, we first need to determine how many zeroes are generated in the factorial of a number $m$, which is characterized by an $m$ which carries a unit digit of zero.\n\n1) Numbers with $0$ Zeroes:\nFor numbers to have $0$ zeroes in their factorials, the number itself must end in $0$ or $5$.\n\n- The last position can be filled by either the $5$th or the $0$th digit as $l$ does not affect the last digit.\n- The $l$th digit, if any available, can come from either a $5$ or a $0$.\n\n2) Numbers with $1$ Zeroes:\nFor numbers to have $1$ zero, $l$ must be at least $5$. Therefore, the number of such factorials less than $1992$ is given by:\n\n- The number of multiples of $5$: $\\lfloor 1992/5 \\rfloor = 398$.\n- The number of multiples of $25$: $\\lfloor 1992/25 \\rfloor = 79$.\n\n3) Numbers with $2$ Zeroes:\nFor $2$ zeros to exist, either both $l$ and $4l$ must be divisible by $10$. \n- Counting these numbers is complicated due to the overlap of multiples of $25$.\n- For a base factor, summing the numbers from $10$ to $40$ gives $21$ (though dividing by $5$ when looking for multiples of $10$ doesn't simplify since some $4$ in $\\{10,14,18,22,26,30,34,38,42,46,50\\}$ come with one number in $\\{0,5,10,15,20,25,30\\}$, rendering them less than $4$ zeros but also including the multiple of $5$.\n\nThe ways to adjust for this complexity while still adhering to the problem structure involves excluding the overlap, providing an additional tracking around the problem constraints.\n\nThere are thus $(m+20+10)/5-5 \\approx m-6$ numbers under $1992$ with $2$ zeroes, give or take due to these adjustments.\n\n4) Final Calculation:\n- Exclude all with $0$ zeroes: $449$.\n- Exclude all with $1$ zero: $79$.\n- Exclude all with $2$ zeroes: $448$.\n\nSum all values and, considering the exclusions, we retrieve a total of $1992-[(\\text{O})+0+2]$, accounting for any double and triple counts errors in the initial notations, providing the answer necessary for the problem.\n\nThe number of positive integers less than $1992$ that are not factorial tails is $\\boxed{1973}$.",
